            <div xml:id="d1367">

                <pb facs="1167" n="1063" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1063"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/598a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                            Brown Brothers &amp; Co. and J. &amp; W. Seligman &amp;
                            Co.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-10-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 27, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department will be glad to have you place two hundred of the four hundred
                    thousand of Nicaragua’s money at their disposal. Immediately a telegraphic reply
                    comes from Nicaragua, you will be advised regarding the arrangement respecting
                    the balance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
